<https://clscor.io/entity/342279a2-ddc5-4d60-b603-0e28337ceba0> a ns1:PC0_Typed_CRM_Property,
        ns1:PC3_has_note,
        rdfs:Resource,
        owl:Thing ;
    ns1:P01_has_domain <https://clscor.io/entity/40b4ac1d60> ;
    ns1:P03_has_range_literal """This tool is not a statistical model / a set of statistical models, but it does include statistical models.
To train a model for UDPipe2 yourself, you would have to set up a UDPipe 2 instance locally and run the source scripts as described here: https://github.com/ufal/udpipe/tree/udpipe-2.   \r
So, theoretically yes, but it is not meant to be performed by users without solid programming background.  \r
If you want to train your model yourself before the release for UDPipe 2, you can easily do so with UDPipe 1, although probably with somewhat lower performance than UDPipe2 would achieve.\r
You are very welcome to contribute to the Universal Dependencies Treebanks. Once your treebank is valid and large enough (10,000 tokens), it will be automatically included in the next version of the models for UDPipe 2.""" ;
    ns1:P3.1_has_type ns2:statistical_models ;
